course: dictionary
lesson: 4917
title: Full immersion
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immersion means putting something completely under water or another liquid. «Baptists and many Pentecostal churches baptise people... usually by full immersion, which means going right under the water.» So full immersion means going all the way under, not just getting your feet wet.
explain: The word has another meaning too: being deeply involved in something. «Language immersion» means learning a language by living in it every day, so you hear and use it all the time. Look at the words around immersion to find which meaning fits.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to choose. In a science lesson, immersion means putting an object in water to see if it floats or sinks. At a school with «French immersion», the lessons themselves are taught in French. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Immersion means putting something completely under water or another liquid.
fact: «Full immersion» means going right under the water, as some churches do when they baptise people.
fact: «Language immersion» means learning a language by being surrounded by it every day.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, an immersion is an electric heater in a water tank that heats hot water.
exercise: «Baptists... usually by full immersion, which means going right under the water.» What does full immersion mean? | *Going right under the water | Standing in a shallow puddle | Singing a hymn while floating | Washing only the hands
exercise: Mia's class is in «French immersion» and learns maths in French. What does immersion suggest here? | Only one French lesson a week | Swimming in a pool | *Being surrounded by French all day, in lessons and play
exercise: In science, Sam puts a stone in a bucket of water to see if it sinks. What does immersion mean in his test? | Drying the stone in the sun | Throwing the stone high into the air | *Putting the stone completely under the water
test: In the UK, what does an immersion heater do? | Makes ice cubes | *Heats the water in a water tank | Lights up the bathroom | Cools the air in a room
test: Ben spends a summer in Spain and speaks only Spanish every day. What is this called? | Full stop | *Language immersion | Deep sea diving | Lost in translation
exam: Which sentence uses immersion to mean being deeply involved in something? | He hid under the water at the swimming pool | The river was in flood after the storm | She ran a bath and sat in it for ten minutes | *She spent a year in total immersion in Irish at her school
